Bugfix: Fix crash with `-o vss.provider` on 32-bit Windows

When `--use-fs-snapshot` was combined with `-o vss.provider` set to a
provider name or ID, restic crashed with an access violation on 32-bit
Windows while looking up the provider. On 64-bit Windows, the same lookup
could overwrite memory. Restic now reads the provider list correctly.

